<p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src="../../images/aaa8-pixel.gif" width="150" height="1"></p></td><td align="left" valign="top" height="375" colspan="2"> 
<!-- #BeginEditable "form" --> <p><font size="+2">Rhode Island Settlers 1760<br> 
</font></p><p>&quot;List of Settlers brought from Newport Rhode Island to Falmouth 
Nov. In the Sloop Sally, Jona Lovatt, Master in May, 1760.</p><p>Family # of persons 
cost<br> Benjimin Sanford and Family 7 &pound;8, 15, 0<br> Nathaniel Reynolds 
and Family 4 &pound;5, 0 , 0<br> Samuel Bently and Family 2 &pound;2, 10, 0<br> 
James Hervie and Family 5 &pound;6, 5 , 0<br> James Smith and Family 6 &pound;7, 
10, 0<br> John Chambers and Family 1 &pound;1, 5 , 0<br> James Weeden and Family 
6 &pound;7, 10, 0<br> Joshua Sanford and Family 3 &pound;3, 15, 0<br> John Hervie 
and Family 1 and family 1, 5 , 0</p><p>In whole 35 Persons<br> 35 persons at &pound;1,5,0 
each is &pound;43,15,0<br> These are to signify that the above is the true and 
perfect list of the settlers brought to the township of Falmouth in the Sloop 
Sally and of the numbers of their families as appears by the ___ of the several 
persons therein named</p><p>(Unsigned)</p><p>List of settlers brought from Newport 
in Rhode Island to Falmouth in the sloop Lydia, Saml Toby, Master, in May, 1760.</p><p>Family 
# of persons <br> Benjimin Burdin and family 3<br> Caleb Lake and family 7<br> 
Henry Tucker and family 3<br> James Mosher and family 8</p><p>23 persons at &pound;1,5,0 
each is &pound;28,15.0</p><p>...Composed by Isaac Deschamps*, then Government 
Agent and Magistrate at Fort Edward, across the river from the Rhode Island Settlements...</p><p> 
<hr noshade> <br> Rhode Island Emigration to Nova Scotia<br> by Ray Greene Huling, 
A.M., New Bedford Massachusetts<br> Providence, R. I., Reprinted from the Narragansett 
Historical Register,<br> April 1889.<br> ISBN 88812 - 215 - 2 Toronto 1984 Canadiana 
House<br> HRL 971.6 H912r 1984 c.2<br> Pg 16 <p>*Deschamps was related by marriage 
to William Haliburton, Thomas Chandler Haliburton's grandfather. - &quot;Family 
Ties&quot; by Gordon M. Haliburton, see bibliography</p><!-- #EndEditable --></td><td valign="top" align="left"> 
<p align="right">&nbsp;</p></td></tr> <tr> <td valign="top" align="left" colspan="5" bgcolor="cccccc"> 
